# MISCHIEF / HIDE — hide-and-seek behind the notch. Derived from base.pet `sit`.
# peek_*, tail_peek_*: the engine parks the sprite so the notch covers cols 0-7;
# cols 0-7 stay empty and the shape runs on behind the notch at col 8 (no k there).
# peek_1/peek_2 alternate (eye glances up-left, ear tip leans back 1 px); peek_grin = ^ eye + blep.
# tail_peek_1/2: only the tail pokes out and wags (tip rises 2 px and curls left; rows 8-15 identical).
# pop: BOO! front view, body 1 px taller (alert layout), paws flung up, mouth open, tail curled as in sit.
# pop is registered to sit (head cols 1-12 as react alert, feet c3-4/c9-10, tail cols 12-15).
# pop: rows 0-8 mirror around the face centre (c6|c7): paws over the cheek edges (c0-1, c12-13), forearms at c0 and c13.

